# One shell command per line, run from the repo root by githooks/pre-push.
# Non-zero exit refuses the push. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This list is exactly what .github/workflows/ci.yml runs, and that is the whole
# point: a check that fails here fails in CI too, so you learn it in seconds
# rather than after a round trip. Adding a step to one and not the other is the
# defect - a local gate that runs a different graph from CI reports a verdict
# about a build nobody is shipping.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: a syntax check on tools/*.py. The tools are dev
# utilities that ship nothing; when story #11 exercises photos.py for real,
# revisit this.
#
# linkcheck walks BOTH sites and reads href AND src, since story #12. It took
# `hq` alone until then, so every file under sailing/ and shared/ was outside
# the gate entirely - including, on the day it was noticed, the whole of the
# lightbox. And it read href only, so a mistyped <script src> passed green and
# degraded to exactly the intended no-JavaScript baseline: a silent failure
# wearing the costume of a supported mode.
#
# The linkcheck line below is python, and it names its interpreter as $PY, not
# as a command. githooks/pre-push resolves $PY once, by RUNNING
# githooks/pyprobe.py under each candidate (CAIRN_PY, python3, python, py, then
# any Python3* under %LOCALAPPDATA%) and taking the first that exits 0. If none
# can run a script, it refuses the push rather than skipping the line. CI sets
# PY=python3 in ci.yml, so both lists carry the same line character for
# character. To run it by hand, run `sh githooks/pre-push`, not the bare line:
# outside the driver $PY is empty.
#
# Why a resolved name and not a spelling: this line said `python3` from
# 2026-09-03, when all of python, python3 and py ran a real interpreter on the
# owner's machine. Measured 2026-09-14, `python3` there is the Windows Store
# alias stub again (126 from sh, 9009 from PowerShell) while `python` and
# `py -3` run a real 3.12.1, so every hand run of this gate failed on this line.
# cairn records this interpreter moving four times, each correction wrong within
# days, which is why the driver resolves it rather than this file naming it.
# Pin one for a single push with CAIRN_PY=/full/path/to/python.
#
# There is no build step. The sites are static files plus the one-line copy in
# the Cloudflare Pages config - see CLAUDE.md.
#
# The photo site joined all three lines in #149. html-validate reads photos/
# through the glob in package.json's `check` script, and refuses an inline
# style there (photos/.htmlvalidate.json), because the site's CSP would drop
# one silently. linkcheck reads photos/public, not photos: that is the site's
# served root, its Pages output directory. `npm run --silent test` runs the
# site's own tests with node --test (photos/test/), which hold the Functions,
# the headers, _routes.json and the Wrangler config.
npm run --silent check
$PY tools/linkcheck.py hq sailing photos/public
npm run --silent test
